# `yo fix --migrate deref` inserts `.*` where a reference is read as a whole
# value of a `Copy` type (b.yo: `take_i(r.*)`). Where the referent is not
# implicitly copyable, `r.*` would be E0901, so the `String` sites (a.yo: a
# by-value argument, c.yo: a `:=` binding) are listed and left as written
# (issues/fixed/2026-11-05-migrate-deref-copies-a-move-only-referent-into-a-by-value-parameter.md;
# `check`'s E0926 text for them is pinned in tests/local_borrows.test.yo).
# One site per file: a file whose evaluation stops (at the E0901 the kept copy
# still raises) is migrated only up to that point. That makes `fix` exit 1,
# and the harness stops a case at its first non-zero command, so no command
# can follow it here.
stdout_keep=^(fix:|error|help)
timeout=240
